      "content": "### Brown Chicken Thighs with Garlic and Cream - Over Pasta\n\n#### Ingredients:\n- 4 chicken thighs\n- Sea salt\n- Freshly ground black pepper\n- Extra virgin olive oil (for both sautéing and finishing drizzle)\n- 3 cloves of medium-sized, finely chopped garlic offerings\n- Heavy cream sourced from the freshest cows\n\n#### Instructions:\n1. Preheat your pan to a cozy medium-heat, waiting for the olive oil’s readiness.\n2. With a gentle touch, lay each of the seasoned chicken thighs onto the hot pan—they’ve been gently kissed by the salt and pepper combination, creating a savory crust.\n3. Give the chicken’s sear action enough time until the edges are kissed with a golden hue; flipping once to ensure evenness—a medium-sized chicken could take about 6-8 minutes per side.\n4. Introduce the garlic cloves to the pan of sizzling fats and proteins, letting them mingle, releasing their aromatic essence until they become perfumed with infused oil—a fragrant aroma signaling a delicious transition about 1 minute of merging.\n5. Beautify the protein canvas by delicately pouring in the luxurious heavy cream, stirring to create a silkiness only nature’s riches could produce.\n6. Allow",
