      "content": "### Brown Chicken Thighs with Garlic and Cream - Over Pasta\n\n#### Ingredients:\n- 4 chicken thighs\n- Sea salt\n- Freshly ground black pepper\n- Extra virgin olive oil (for both sautéing and finishing drizzle)\n- 3 cloves of medium-sized, finely diced garlic\n- Heavy cream\n\n#### Instructions:\n1. Heat 2 tablespoons of extra virgin olive oil in a wide, durable pan over medium heat.\n2. Season the chicken thighs evenly with sea salt and freshly ground black pepper, making sure each side is equally covered for even flavor.\n3. Sear the chicken thighs skin-side down for 4-5 minutes, until a golden-brown crust forms on the skin. Flip each thigh carefully and cook the other side for another 3-4 minutes, until fully cooked medium-rare.\n4. While the chicken is cooking, mince 3 cloves of garlic and set aside.\n5. Once the chicken is done and removed from the pan, pour 1 cup of heavy cream into the pan, stirring until it comes to a gentle simmer. Let the cream reduce slightly for added richness.\n6. Return the chicken thighs to the pan, nestling them into the creamy sauce. Let the chicken soak up",
